* =================================================
*  PHYSICS QUESTIONS
* =================================================
L:PHYSICS
T:
T:  ---- CATEGORY 1: PHYSICS ----
T:
T:  Q1. What is the SI unit of electrical
T:      resistance?
A:
M:ohm|ohms
MT:  >> CORRECT! Resistance is measured in Ohms.
T:     Answer: Ohm (symbol: the Greek letter Omega)
T:     Ohm's Law: V = I x R
T:     1 Ohm = the resistance that produces 1 Volt
T:     when 1 Ampere of current flows through it.
T:     Named after Georg Simon Ohm (1789-1854).
T:
T:  Q2. What fundamental force keeps planets
T:      in orbit around the Sun?
A:
M:gravity|gravitational|gravitation
MT:  >> CORRECT! Gravity governs orbital motion.
T:     Answer: Gravity (Gravitational Force)
T:     Newton's Law of Gravitation:
T:       F = G x m1 x m2 / r^2
T:     Without gravity, planets would travel in
T:     straight lines at constant speed.
T:
T:  Q3. What quantity is measured in Joules?
A:
M:energy|work
MT:  >> CORRECT! The Joule measures energy and work.
T:     Answer: Energy (and Work)
T:     1 Joule = 1 Newton-meter = 1 kg*m^2/s^2
T:     A food Calorie is approximately 4,184 Joules.
T:     Lifting an apple one meter takes about 1 Joule.
T:
E:

* =================================================
*  CHEMISTRY QUESTIONS
* =================================================
L:CHEMISTRY
T:
T:  ---- CATEGORY 2: CHEMISTRY ----
T:
T:  Q4. What is the chemical symbol for gold?
A:
M:Au|au
MT:  >> CORRECT! Gold's symbol comes from Latin.
T:     Answer: Au (from Latin "Aurum" -- shining dawn)
T:     Gold is element 79, atomic mass 196.97.
T:     It is one of the least reactive elements and
T:     has been prized by civilizations for millennia.
T:
T:  Q5. What is the pH value of a perfectly
T:      neutral solution?
A:
M:7|seven
MT:  >> CORRECT! pH 7 is neutral.
T:     Answer: 7
T:     The pH scale runs from 0 (strongly acidic)
T:     to 14 (strongly alkaline/basic).
T:     Pure water at 25 C has a pH of exactly 7.
T:     Each pH unit = a tenfold change in H+ ions.
T:
T:  Q6. What is the most abundant gas in
T:      Earth's atmosphere?
A:
M:nitrogen|N2|n2
MT:  >> CORRECT! Nitrogen dominates our atmosphere.
T:     Answer: Nitrogen (N2) -- about 78% by volume
T:     Oxygen is second at about 21%.
T:     Argon makes up most of the remaining 1%.
T:     Nitrogen is essential for amino acids and DNA.
T:
E:

* =================================================
*  BIOLOGY QUESTIONS
* =================================================
L:BIOLOGY
T:
T:  ---- CATEGORY 3: BIOLOGY ----
T:
T:  Q7. What organelle is known as the
T:      "powerhouse of the cell"?
A:
M:mitochondria|mitochondrion
MT:  >> CORRECT! Mitochondria power the cell.
T:     Answer: Mitochondria (singular: Mitochondrion)
T:     They produce ATP through cellular respiration.
T:     Mitochondria have their own DNA, inherited
T:     from the maternal line. A typical human cell
T:     contains 1,000 to 2,000 mitochondria.
T:
T:  Q8. What molecule carries the genetic
T:      instructions for all living organisms?
A:
M:DNA|deoxyribonucleic
MT:  >> CORRECT! DNA stores genetic information.
T:     Answer: DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)
T:     Its double-helix structure was described by
T:     Watson and Crick in 1953. Human DNA contains
T:     approximately 3 billion base pairs. Uncoiled,
T:     one cell's DNA would stretch about 2 meters.
T:
T:  Q9. What process do plants use to convert
T:      sunlight into chemical energy?
A:
M:photosynthesis
MT:  >> CORRECT! Photosynthesis converts light energy.
T:     Answer: Photosynthesis
T:     6CO2 + 6H2O + light --> C6H12O6 + 6O2
T:     It takes place in chloroplasts using the
T:     pigment chlorophyll. Photosynthesis produces
T:     the oxygen that most life on Earth depends on.
T:
E:

* =================================================
*  EARTH SCIENCE QUESTIONS
* =================================================
L:EARTHSCI
T:
T:  ---- CATEGORY 4: EARTH SCIENCE ----
T:
T:  Q10. What scale is commonly used to measure
T:       earthquake magnitude?
A:
M:richter|moment magnitude
MT:  >> CORRECT! Earthquakes are measured on magnitude scales.
T:      Answer: Richter Scale / Moment Magnitude Scale
T:      Charles Richter developed his scale in 1935.
T:      Each whole number increase represents 10x more
T:      ground shaking and about 31.6x more energy.
T:      The 2011 Tohoku earthquake measured 9.1 Mw.
T:
T:  Q11. What layer of the atmosphere contains
T:       the protective ozone layer?
A:
M:stratosphere
MT:  >> CORRECT! The ozone layer resides in the stratosphere.
T:      Answer: Stratosphere (10-50 km altitude)
T:      The ozone layer absorbs 97-99% of harmful UV.
T:      CFCs depleted it, but the 1987 Montreal Protocol
T:      has allowed it to begin recovering. Full recovery
T:      is projected by approximately 2066.
T:
T:  Q12. What type of rock is formed from cooled
T:       magma or lava?
A:
M:igneous
MT:  >> CORRECT! Igneous rock forms from cooled magma.
T:      Answer: Igneous Rock (from Latin "ignis" = fire)
T:      Intrusive: cools slowly underground (e.g., granite)
T:      Extrusive: cools quickly at surface (e.g., basalt)
T:      About 65% of Earth's crust is igneous rock.
T:      The three rock types are igneous, sedimentary,
T:      and metamorphic.
T:
E:

* =================================================
*  ASTRONOMY QUESTIONS
* =================================================
L:ASTRONOMY
T:
T:  ---- CATEGORY 5: ASTRONOMY ----
T:
T:  Q13. What is the closest star to Earth?
A:
M:sun|sol|the sun
MT:  >> CORRECT! Our Sun is the nearest star.
T:      Answer: The Sun (Sol)
T:      Distance: ~150 million km (1 Astronomical Unit)
T:      Surface temperature: about 5,500 degrees C
T:      The next nearest star is Proxima Centauri
T:      at 4.24 light-years away.
T:
T:  Q14. What planet in our solar system is
T:       famous for its prominent ring system?
A:
M:saturn
MT:  >> CORRECT! Saturn's rings are iconic.
T:      Answer: Saturn
T:      Saturn's rings are made mostly of ice particles
T:      ranging from tiny grains to house-sized chunks.
T:      The ring system spans up to 282,000 km but is
T:      only about 10 meters thick on average.
T:      Saturn also has 146 confirmed moons.
T:
T:  Q15. Approximately how old is the universe
T:       (in billions of years)?
A:
M:13|13.8|fourteen|13.8 billion
MT:  >> CORRECT! The universe is about 13.8 billion years old.
T:      Answer: ~13.8 billion years
T:      Determined by measurements of the cosmic
T:      microwave background radiation (CMB).
T:      The observable universe is about 93 billion
T:      light-years in diameter due to expansion.
T:      The first stars formed ~200 million years
T:      after the Big Bang.
T:
E:
